2026-11-21T05:46:57 | Claude chunk persisted-index | decision | Design: IndexFile.cs holds one JSON per repo under Paths.Index (<name>-<hash12>.json: version, repo, savedAt, statuses, folders[relative dir, archived, racy, stamps[path/size/mtime UTC ISO], parsed item with Path blanked]). ItemsCache seeds an Entry from it (Unverified flag) so Register paints with no read; the headers step calls ItemsCache.Verify(), which is the normal listing+stamp compare. Index saved at end of load (if dirty), after RebuildIndex, and by Workspace.SaveIndexes() on exit; never mid-load. Index folder is injectable via ItemsCache.State.IndexFolder (Paths.Home is a static).\nWhy: Paths.Home is read once from RTM_HOME at static init so tests cannot redirect it; killed apps (the startup script) never reach the exit hook, so the end of load also saves.
2026-11-21T05:48:06 | Claude chunk persisted-index | tests-red | Wrote TaskManager.Tests/KeepingAnIndexBetweenRunsTests.cs (6 facts per the brief). Red: IndexFile, ItemsCache.State.IndexFolder, Workspace.RebuildIndex and SaveIndexes do not exist yet (does not compile).
2026-11-21T05:49:53 | Claude chunk verify-not-refresh | decision | Verify lives in OpenSpecStore/Verification.cs (store cannot call TaskManager's ItemsCache.Fingerprint): one listing of changes/, specs/ and config.yaml vs held per-file stamps; differing paths go into the store's touched record so ItemsCache re-reads exactly those folders, config re-reads only when its path differs. Own writes adopt their stamps in Touch().\nWhy: dependency direction, and it makes the racy rule and 'read only what differs' hold end to end.
