2026-11-21T05:56:44 | Claude chunk write-through | found | Symptom: not reproduced where the call and the window share one repository. A bUnit board plus BoardTools.BoardCreate (AfterWrite = Notify) shows the card, and the hidden app (CDP, board view, before any fix) shows the tool-created item in Planned within 3 s (112 to 113 cards). Path read: tool write -> Touch bumps Repo.Version -> AfterWrite -> Notify -> Changed -> RepoPage reload -> ItemsCache.Board (cache hit only while Version is unchanged). Loss candidates: (1) the call lands in a repo the app has not got open: FindRepoRoot of a worktree/junction path gives another root, InRepo makes it a GUEST, the write goes to that tree and bumps the guest's Version only, so the open repo's cache is a hit and the page re-reads the old board while board_list (same guest) lists the item; (2) the page's one-shot own-echo skip, ruled out because Stamp() includes TotalVersion. The owner's log shows BoardCreate calls but no repo root in the trace line; I add it.
